        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "6316f6a6-170d-5c26-b6fe-b472e858283c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Hans Schlegel, Frank De Winne, Dirk Frimout\n- Organizations: ESA, NASA, ISS, Roscosmos\n- Events: Expedition 21, Expedition 35, NASA Space Shuttle missions\n- Roles: astronaut, physicist, Belgian Air Component officer, ISS commander\n\nFacts:\n- Hans Wilhelm Schlegel was born in Überlingen on 3 August 1951.\n- Frank De Winne was born in Ledeberg, Belgium, on 25 April 1961.\n- Hans Schlegel is a German physicist, an ESA astronaut, and a veteran of two NASA Space Shuttle missions.\n- Frank De Winne is a Belgian Air Component officer and an ESA astronaut.\n- Frank De Winne was Belgium's second person in space after Dirk Frimout.\n- In 2009, Frank De Winne became the first ESA astronaut to command a space mission when he served as commander of ISS Expedition 21.\n- Expedition 35 was only the second time an ISS crew was led by neither a NASA astronaut nor a Roscosmos cosmonaut, after Expedition 21 in 2009 under Frank De Winne's command.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
